t's side of the boundary; the agent container must never see it.[K[1B[K[2C[1B[1mThe real consequence for what we built[1B[22m[K[2C[1BIf[6Gyou[10Glock[15Gthe[19Gcontainer[29Gdown[34Gproperly,[44G[1marteries can't reach the database from inside it.[94G[22mAnd[98G[38;2;177;185;249mlog_event[108G[39mdegrades[117Gsilently[126G—[128Git[131Gfalls[137Gback[142Gto[145GJSONL[151Gwritten[159Ginto[164Gthe[168Gcontainer's[180Gfilesystem,[192Gwhich[198Gdies[203Gwith[208Gthe[212Gcontainer.[223GEvery[229Gsubtask's[239Gmemory[246Gand[2C[1Btelemetry, lost, with[25Gno[28Gerror.[2B [3GYou already have[20Gthe right channel for this: the [1mspool[22m.[59G[38;2;177;185;249mspool_emit[39m appends NDJSON to [38;2;177;185;249mHEART_SPOOL_DIR[39m (d[107Gfault [38;2;177;185;249m~/.local/share/heart/events[39m),[143Gone[147Gfile[152Gper[156Gday,[161Gappend-only,[174Gand[178Git's[183Gdescribed[193Gas[196Gthe[200Gshared[207Gspine[213Gfor[217Gheart,[224Garteries,[234Gand[238Gmarrow.[246GA[2C[1Bbind-mounted[16Gspool[22Gdirectory[32Gis[35Ga[37Gnarrow,[45Gcredential-free,[62Gwrite-only[73Gchannel[81G—[83Gthe[87Gcontainer[97Gappends,[106Ga[108Ghost-side[118Greader[125Gingests[133Ginto[138GPostgres.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BSo[6Gthe[10Gpattern[18Gbecomes:[27G[1minside the sandbox, arteries writes to the spool; outside, heart drains the spool into the database.[128G[22mNo[131GDB[134Gcredentials[146Gcross[152Gthe[156Gboundary[165Gat[168Gall.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BTha[7G needs a[16Gdecision from you, because today the spool[59Gis best-effort decora[81Gion and Postgre[97G is the source of truth. For[126Gsandboxed[136Gruns[141Gthose[147Groles[153Ginvert.[161GIt's[166Gnot[170Ga[172Glarge[178Gchange,[186Gbut[190Git's[195Gthe[199Gpiece[205Gthat[210Ghas[214Gto[217Gexist[223Gbefore[230G[38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[241G[39mis[244Guseful.[2C[2B[1mShutdown, in layers[22m[K[2C[2B"Shut down accordingly" needs more than one mechanism, because the failure modes differ:[2C[2B- [1mResource limits[22m (cgroups: memory, CPU, pids, d[52Gsk)[56Ghandle the mal[71Gunc[75Gion case — a runaway[96Gsubtask[104Ggets[109Gkilled[116Gby[119Gthe[123Gkernel,[131Gnot[135Gby[138Ga[140Gwatchdog[149Gthat[154Gmight[160Gitself[167Gbe[170Gwedged.[2C[1B-[5G[1mA wall-clock timeout[26G[22mon[29Gthe[33Gcontainer[43Ghandles[51Gthe[55Ghang.[2C[1B- [1mEgres[11G denial[22m handles exposure without needing to detect anything — the safest[84Gcontrol is the one[103Gthat[108Gdoesn'[115G require [125Goticing.[K[2C[1B- [1mHeart, outside the container[22m, watches exit and closes[59Gthe[63Garteries runs. Container exit i[95G still your most[112Grel[116Gable [122Gnd signal.[K[2C[1B-[5G[1mThe idle sweep[20G[22mremains[28Gthe[32Gbackstop[41Gfor[45Gwhen[50Gheart[56Gitself[63Gdies.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BDetection-based[19Gshutdown[28G("notice[37Git[40Gdoing[46Gsomething[56Gbad,[61Gthen[66Gkill[71Git")[76Gis[79Gthe[83Gweakest[91Gof[94Gthese[100Gand[104GI'd[108Gnot[112Gbuild[118Git[121Gfirst.[128GPrevention[139Gthat[144Gcan't[150Gbe[153Gevaded[160Gbeats[166Gmonitoring[177Gthat[182Gcan.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOne thing worth reconsidering[22m[K[2C[2BDocker shares the host kernel, so a container [50Gscape is a kernel exploit away. For a[88G [3maccidental[23m thr[104Gat model — a subtask[125Gthat [38;2;177;185;249mrm -rf[137G[39m the wrong path[153Gor pip-installs something malicious — Docker plus[203Gthe hardening above is proporti[235Gnate.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BIf[6Gyou[10Glater[16Gwant[21Gto[24Grun[28Ggenuinely[38Guntrusted[48Gprompts,[57GgVisor[64Gor[67Ga[69GmicroVM[77G(Firecracker,[91GKata)[97Ggives[103Gyou[107Ga[109Greal[114Gkernel[121Gboundary[130Gat[133Gmeaningful[144Gcost.[150GWarren's[159Gprovider[168Gseam[173Gis[176Gthe[180Greason[187Gto[190Gbuild[196Gthat[201Gabstraction[213Gnow[217Geven[222Gif[225Gyou[229Gonly[234Gimplement[244GDocker:[2C[1B[1mmake [38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[39m o[21Ge implemen[32Gation of "give me an isolated workspace," not a hardcoded path in heart.[105G[22mThen[110Gupgrading[120Gthe[124Gisolation[134Gstrength[143Glater[149Gtouches[157Gone[161Gfile,[167Gand[171Grunning[179Gan[182Gepisode[190Gunsandboxed[202Gstays[208Gpossible[217Gfor[221Glocal[227Gdevelopment[239G—[241Gas[244Gan[247Gexplicit[2C[1Bopt-out,[12Gnever[18Gthe[22Gdefault.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mRevised recommendation[22m[K[2C[2BUnch[8Gng[11Gd on grain: one sandbox per episode,[48Gsubtasks as processes[70Ginside with their[88Gown [38;2;177;185;249mARTERIES_RUN_ID[39m.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BAdded,[10Gin[13Gorder[19Gof[22Gwhat[27GI'd[31Gbuild[37Gfirst:[2C[1B[K[2C[1B1.[6GEgress[13Gallowlist[23Gand[27Gno[30Ghost[35Gmounts[42Gbeyond[49Gthe[53Gworktree[62G—[64Gthe[68Gcontrols[77Gthat[82Gdon't[88Gdepend[95Gon[98Gdetection[2C[1B2. Spool-as-channel so arteries[35Gworks from insid[53Gwithout DB credentials[K[2C[1B3.[6Gcgroup[13Glimits[20Gand[24Ga[26Gwall-clock[37Gtimeout[2C[1B4. Provider seam so[23Gthe[27Gisolation[37Gbackend[45Gis[48Gswappable[2C[1B5.[6GHeart[12Gclosing[20Gruns[25Gon[28Gcontainer[38Gexit[2C[1B[K[2C[1BWant[8Gme[11Gto[14Gwrite[20Gup[23Gthe[27Gspool-drain[39Gpath,[45Gsince[51Gthat's[58Gthe[62Gpiece[68Garteries[77Gactually[86Gneeds[92Gand[96Gthe[100Gonly[105Gone[109Gthat[114Gtouches[122Gcode[127Gwe've[133Galready[141Gchanged?[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GCrunched for 1m 17s · 2 shells still running[39m[K[2C[1B[K[1B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mAlso analyze https://github.com/AgentSystemLabs/mission-control[39m                                                                                          