3;153m1.6k tokens)[39m[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[52B[38;2;215;119;87m·[3G[38;2;220;129;97mSpinning…[39m[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[3GYou already have the [25Gight channel fo[41G this: the [1mspool[22m. [38;2;177;185;249mspool_emit[39m appends NDJSON to [38;2;177;185;249mHEART_SPOOL_DIR[39m (defaul[112G [38;2;177;185;249m~/.local/share/heart/events[39m), one file[152Gper[156Gday,[161Gappend-only,[174Gand[178Git's[183Gdescribed[193Gas[196Gthe[200Gshared[207Gspine[213Gfor[217Gheart,[224Garteries,[234Gand[238Gmarrow.[246GA[2C[1Bbind-mounted[16Gspool[22Gdirectory[32Gis[35Ga[37Gnarrow,[45Gcredential-free,[62Gwrite-only[73Gchannel[81G—[83Gthe[87Gcontainer[97Gappends,[106Ga[108Ghost-side[118Greader[125Gingests[133Ginto[138GPostgres.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BSo[6Gthe[10Gpattern[18Gbecomes:[27G[1minside the sandbox, arteries writes to the spool; outside, heart drains the spool into the database.[128G[22mNo[131GDB[134Gcredentials[146Gcross[152Gthe[156Gboundary[165Gat[168Gall.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BThat[8Gneeds[14Ga[16Gdecision[25Gfrom[30Gyou,[35Gbecause[43Gtoday[49Gthe[53Gspool[59Gis[62Gbest-effort[74Gdecoration[85Gand[89GPostgres[98Gis[101Gthe[105Gsource[112Gof[115Gtruth.[122GFor[126Gsandboxed[136Gruns[141Gthose[147Groles[153Ginvert.[161GIt's[166Gnot[170Ga[172Glarge[178Gchange,[186Gbut[190Git's[195Gthe[199Gpiece[205Gthat[210Ghas[214Gto[217Gexist[223Gbefore[230G[38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[241G[39mis[244Guseful.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mShutdown, in layers[2C[1B[22m[K[2C[1B"Shut[9Gdown[14Gaccordingly"[27Gneeds[33Gmore[38Gthan[43Gone[47Gmechanism,[58Gbecause[66Gthe[70Gfailure[78Gmodes[84Gdiffer:[2C[1B[K[4C[1B[1mResource limi[19Gs[22m (cgroups: mem[35Gry, CPU, pi[47Gs, disk) handle[63Gthe[67Gmalfunction[79Gcase[84G—[86Ga[88Grunaway[96Gsubtask[104Ggets[109Gkilled[116Gby[119Gthe[123Gkernel,[131Gnot[135Gby[138Ga[140Gwatchdog[149Gthat[154Gmight[160Gitself[167Gbe[170Gwedged.[4C[1B[1mA wall-clock timeout[22m on the container handles the[55Ghang.[K[4C[1B[1mEgress[12Gdenial[22m handles exposure wit[40Gout needi[50Gg[52Gto d[57Gtect any[66Ghing — the safest control is the one that doesn't require noticing.[4C[1B[1mHeart, outside the container[22m, wa[38Gches exit and closes the[63Garteries[72Gruns.[78GContainer[88Gexit[93Gis[96Gstill[102Gyour[107Gmost[112Greliable[121Gend[125Gsignal.[2C[1B-[5G[1mThe idle sweep[20G[22mremains[28Gthe[32Gbackstop[41Gfor[45Gwhen[50Gheart[56Gitself[63Gdies.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BDetection-based[19Gshutdown[28G("notice[37Git[40Gdoing[46Gsomething[56Gbad,[61Gthen[66Gkill[71Git")[76Gis[79Gthe[83Gweakest[91Gof[94Gthese[100Gand[104GI'd[108Gnot[112Gbuild[118Git[121Gfirst.[128GPrevention[139Gthat[144Gcan't[150Gbe[153Gevaded[160Gbeats[166Gmonitoring[177Gthat[182Gcan.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOne thing worth reconsidering[2C[1B[22m[K[2C[1BDocker[10Gshares[17Gthe[21Ghost[26Gkernel,[34Gso[37Ga[39Gcontainer[49Gescape[56Gis[59Ga[61Gkernel[68Gexploit[76Gaway.[82GFor[86Gan[89G[3maccidental[100G[23mthreat[107Gmodel[113G—[115Ga[117Gsubtask[125Gthat[130G[38;2;177;185;249mrm -rf[39ms[138Gthe[142Gwrong[148Gpath[153Gor[156Gpip-installs[169Gsomething[179Gmalicious[189G—[191GDocker[198Gplus[203Gthe[207Ghardening[217Gabove[223Gis[226Gproportionate.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BIf you later want to run genuinely untrusted prompts, gVisor or a microVM (Firecracker, Kata) gives you a real ker[118Gel boundary at meani[140Gful cost. Warr[155Gn's provider seam is the reason to[190Gbuild that abstraction now[217Geven if you on[232Gy implement[244GDocker:[K[2C[1B[1mmake [38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[39m one implementation of "give me an isolated workspace," not a hardcoded path in heart.[105G[22mThen[110Gupgrading[120Gthe[124Gi