B[1mSandbox is a runtime, not a scope.[38G[22mTheir[44Gearlier[52Gdesign[59Gmade[64Geach[69Gsandbox[77Ga[79Gsecond[86Gproject[94Grow[98Gand[102Gfiltered[111Gproject[119Glists[125Gby[128Gactive[135Gsandbox.[144GThey[149Gcall[154Gthat[159Gout[163Gas[166Gwrong:[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[2m▎[5G[22m[3m"The original project remains the project. A project sandbox is linked to the project that created it with [38;2;177;185;249mprojectId[39m. Switching Local/sandbox changes the active runtime for that project, not the project list."[2C[1B[23m[K[2C[1BThat's[10Gyour[15Grun-versus-container[36Gdistinction[48Gstated[55Gin[58Gtheir[64Gvocabulary.[76GA[78Gsandbox[86Gis[89G[3mwhere[95G[23mwork[100Gexecutes;[110Git[113Gisn't[119Ga[121Gnew[125Gidentity[134Gfor[138Gthe[142Gwork.[148GYour[153Gepisode[161Gstays[167Gthe[171Gepisode[179Gwhether[187Git[190Gruns[195Gin[198Ga[200Gcontainer[210Gor[213Ga[215Gbare[220Gworktree[229G—[231Gwhich[237Gis[240Gexactly[248Gwhy[252GI'd[2C[1Bkeep [38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[39m b[21Ghind a provider seam rather [50Ghan letting it become a new[78Gaxis in[86Gyour data model.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mIdle auto-stop is the industry answer to your shutdown requirement.[71G[22mTheir[77GVMs[81Gdefault[89Gto[92Ga[94G30-minute[104Gidle[109Gtimeout.[118GThat's[125Gthe[129Gsame[134Gshape[140Gas[143Gthe[147Gsweep[153Gyou[157Gjust[162Gbuilt,[169Gat[172Ga[174Gdifferent[184Glayer[190G—[192Gand[196Gnotably[204Gnot[208Gdetection-based.[225GTime[230Gis[233Gthe[237Gcontrol[245Geveryone[2C[1Breaches for, because it can't be evaded by the thing you're containing.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mProvider abstraction, honestly scored.[42G[22mThe[46GDigitalOcean[59Gplan[64Grates[70Gtheir[76Gown[80Gcurrent[88Gabstraction[100Gat[103G[3m"~2.5/10 — AWS is inlined across CLI, Electron, types, and UI."[167G[23mThey're[175Gpaying[182Gfor[186Ghaving[