dboxes"[164G[23mand[168Gproduced[177G[38;2;177;185;249mdocker compose up failed (exit 1). See logs.[222G[39mThey[227Gchose[233Gone[237Gpath[242G—[244Gremote[251GVM[254G—[2C[1Brather[10Gthan[15Gmaintain[24Gtwo.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mThree things worth taking[2C[2BSandbox is a runtime, not a scope.[22m Their earlier design made each sandbox a second project row and filt[107Gred[111Gpr[114Gject lists by active sandbox. They call that out as wrong:[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[2m▎[5G[22m[3m"The original project remains the project. A project sandbox is linked to the project that created it with [38;2;177;185;249mprojectId[39m. Switching Local/sandbox changes the active runtime for that project, not the project list."[2C[1B[23m[K[2C[1BThat's[10Gyour[15Grun-versus-container[36Gdistinction[48Gstated[55Gin[58Gtheir[64Gvocabulary.[76GA[78Gsandbox[86Gis[89G[3mwhere[95G[23mwork[100Gexecutes;[110Git[113Gisn't[119Ga[121Gnew[125Gidentity[134Gfor[138Gthe[142Gwork.[148GYour[153Gepisode[161Gstays[167Gthe[171Gepisode[179Gwhether[187Git[190Gruns[195Gin[198Ga[200Gcontainer[210Gor[213Ga[215Gbare[220Gworktree[229G—[231Gwhich[237Gis[240Gexactly[248Gwhy[252GI'd[2C[1Bkeep [38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[39m behind a provider seam [43Gather than letting it become a new axis in[86Gyour data model.[K[2C[2B[1mIdle auto-stop is the industry answer to your shutdown requirement.[22m Their VMs default to a 30-minute idle timeout. That's the same shape as the sweep you just built, at a different layer — and notably not detection-based.[225GTime[230Gis[233Gthe[237Gcontrol[245Geveryone[2C[1Breaches[11Gfor,[16Gbecause[24Git[27Gcan't[33Gbe[36Gevaded[43Gby[46Gthe[50Gthing[56Gyou're[63Gcontaining.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mProvider abstraction, honestly scored.[42G[22mThe Digit[52GlOc[56Gan plan rates their own current abstracti[98Gn at[103G[3m"~2.5/10 — AWS is inlined across CLI, Electron, types, and UI."[167G[23mThey're[175Gpaying[182Gfor[186Ghaving[193Gbuilt[199Gone[203Gprovider[212Gdirectly[221Ginstead[229Gof[232Gbehind[239Ga[241Gseam.[247GThat's[2C[1Bthe[7Gconcrete[16Gcost[21Gof[24Gthe[28Gshortcut[37GWarren[44Gavoided,[53Gdocumented[64Gby[67Gthe[71Gpeople[78Gpaying[85Git.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mHow this changes the recommendation[22m[K[2C[2B[1mNot on gr[13Gin.[22m Nothing here argues against one sandbox per episod[68G.[70G[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mIt does argue against making local Docker your only path.[61G[22mTwo[65Gof[68Gthree[74Gprojects[83Greached[91Gfor[95Gsomething[105Gother[111Gthan[116Ga[118Glocal[124Gcontainer:[135GWarren[142Goffers[149GDocker[156Gbut[160Gtreats[167Git[170Gas[173Gone[177Gof[180Gthree[186Gproviders,[197Gand[201GMission[209GControl[217Gtried[223Glocal[229GDocker[236Gand[240Gremoved[248Git.[2C[1BNeither did so for security reasons[39G—[41Git[44Gwas[48Goperational[60Gfriction[69G—[71Gbut[75Gthe[79Gpattern[87Gis[90Gconsistent[101Genough[108Gto[111Gplan[116Gfor.[2C[2BFor your [3mstated[23m [21Great model, though, remote VMs are worse, not better.[75GMission[83GControl's[93Gsandboxes[103Gprotect[111Gagainst[119Gnothing[127Gthat[132Gmatters[140Gto[143Gyou:[148Gthey're[156Gyour[161Gown[165GEC2[169Ginstance[178Grunning[186Gyour[191Gcode[196Gwith[201Gyour[206Gkeys.[212GWhat[217Gyou[221Gwant[226Gis[229Ga[231Gboundary[240Gbetween[248Gthe[2C[1Bagent[9Gand[13G[3mthis machine[26G[23m—[28Gyour[33GPostgres[42Gpeer-auth[52Gsocket,[60Gyour[65G[38;2;177;185;249m~/.ssh[39m,[73Gyour[78G[38;2;177;185;249m~/.claude[88G[39mcredentials.[101GA[103Glocal[109Gcontainer[119Gwith[124Gno[127Ghost[132Gmounts[139Gand[143Gdefault-deny[156Gegress[163Ggives[169Gyou[173Gthat.[179GAn[182GEC2[186Gbox[190Ggives[196Gyou[200Ga[202Gdifferent[212Gmachine,[221Gwhich[227Gis[230Ga[232Greal[237Gboundary,[247Gat[250Gthe[2C[1Bcost of latency, spend, and moving your entire memory stack [64Gr exposing it over[83Gthe n[89Gtwork.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BSo:[7G[1mbuild [38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[39m, and build it behind the provider seam.[64G[22mThe[68Gseam[73Gis[76Gwhat[81Gall[85Gthree[91Gprojects[100Geither[107Ghave[112G(Warren),[122Gregret[129Gnot[133Ghaving[140G(Mission[149GControl,[158Gself-scored[170G2.5/10),[179Gor[182Gdon't[188Gneed[193Gbecause[201Gthey[206Gnever[212Gsandboxed[222Gat[225Gall[229G(Orca).[237GIt[240Gcosts[246Gyou[250Gone[2C[1Binterface today[19Gand buys the option to add a[48Gremote VM or a[63GmicroVM later without touching heart or[103Ga[105Gteries.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BS[5Gurces:[K[2C[1B-[5G]8;id=i1tesd;https://github.com/AgentSystemLabs/mission-control[94mAgentSystemLabs/mission-control[37G]8;;[39m—[39G]8;id=j09gni;https://github.com/AgentSystemLabs/mission-control/blob/main/daytona-hosted-removal-plan.md[94mdaytona-hosted-removal-plan.md]8;;[39m,[71G]8;id=fnpjv3;https://github.com/AgentSystemLabs/mission-control/blob/main/docs/project-sandbox-aws-flow.md[94mdocs/project-sandbox-aws-flow.md]8;;[39m,[105G]8;id=z2562j;https://github.com/AgentSystemLabs/mission-control/blob/main/docs/digitalocean-sandboxes-plan.md[94mdocs/digitalocean-sandboxes-plan.md]8;;[2C[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GWorked for 1m 28s · 2 shells still running[46G[39m[K[2B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mConsolidate these insights with what we talked about for breaking down episodes/runs from plexus to arteries so I can understand where docker-sbx fits in for security, transferring enough context into each sandbox in least privilege style and helping [39m [1B  [38;2;255;255;255mdistance away from my actual system[39m                                                                                                                                 