t's[2C[1Bthe concrete[16Gcost of[24Gthe shortcut W[39Grren avoided, document[62Gd by the people[78Gpaying[85Git.[2C[2B[1mHow this[12Gchanges the recommendati[37Gn[22m[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mNot on grain.[17G[22mNothing[25Ghere[30Gargues[37Gagainst[45Gone[49Gsandbox[57Gper[61Gepisode.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mIt does argue against making local Docker your only path.[61G[22mTwo[65Gof[68Gthree[74Gprojects[83Greached[91Gfor[95Gsomething[105Gother[111Gthan[116Ga[118Glocal[124Gcontainer:[135GWarren[142Goffers[149GDocker[156Gbut[160Gtreats[167Git[170Gas[173Gone[177Gof[180Gthree[186Gproviders,[197Gand[201GMission[209GControl[217Gtried[223Glocal[229GDocker[236Gand[240Gremoved[248Git.[2C[1BNeither did so for security [32Geasons — it was operational friction —[71Gbut[75Gthe[79Gpattern[87Gis[90Gconsistent[101Genough[108Gto[111Gplan[116Gfor.[2C[2BFor your [3mstated[23m threat model, though, remote VMs are worse, not bett[72Gr. Mission[83GControl's sandboxes pr[107Gect[111Gag[114Ginst nothing [128Ghat matte[138Gs to you: they're[156Gyour own EC2 in[172Gta[175Gce running[186Gyour code with[201Gyour keys. What[217Gyou want is[229Ga bound[237Gry[240Gb[242Gtwe[246Gn[248Gthe[2C[1Bagent an[12G [3mthis machine[23m — you[32G Postgres peer-auth socket,[60Gyour [38;2;177;185;249m~/.ssh[39m, your [38;2;177;185;249m~/.claude[39m credentials.[101GA local cont[114Giner with[124Gno[127Ghost[132Gmounts[139Gand[143Gdefault-deny[156Gegress[163Ggives[169Gyou[173Gthat.[179GAn[182GEC2[186Gbox[190Ggives[196Gyou[200Ga[202Gdifferent[212Gmachine,[221Gwhich[227Gis[230Ga[232Greal[237Gboundary,[247Gat[250Gthe[2C[1Bcost[8Gof[11Glatency,[20Gspend,[27Gand[31Gmoving[38Gyour[43Gentire[50Gmemory[57Gstack[63Gor[66Gexposing[75Git[78Gover[83Gthe[87Gnetwork.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BSo: [1mbuild [38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[39m, and build it behind the provider seam.