rains, four names.[28G[22mPlexus[35Gnames[41Gthe[45Gepisode,[54Gheart[60Gsplits[67Git[70Ginto[75Gsubtasks[84Gand[88Gassigns[96Ga[98Grun[102Gid[105Gper[109Gsubtask,[118Gdocker-sbx[129Gcontains[138Gthe[142Gepisode,[151Garteries[160Gremembers[170Geach[175Gsubtask[183Gseparately.[195GThe[199Gcontainer[209Gis[212Gthe[216Gonly[221Gone[225Gof[228Gthe[232Gfour[237Gwith[242Gno[245Gidentity[2C[1Bof its own — it's a runtime, not [37G scope.[45GThat's Mission[60GControl's[70Gharde[76Gt-won lesson: they modeled sandboxes [115G project scopes, and had to und[147G it.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mThe container wraps the episode, not the subtask.[53G[22mSubtasks[62Galready[70Gshare[76Ga[78Gfilesystem[89Gby[92Gdesign[99G—[101Gthe[105Gfix[109Gagent[115Gneeds[121Gwhat[126Gthe[130Gcoder[136Gwrote.[143GAnd[147Gper-subtask[159Gcontainers[170Gbuy[174Gno[177Gsecurity,[187Gbecause[195Gevery[201Gsubtask[209Ghas[213Gidentical[223Gpermissions[235Gagainst[243Gthe[247Gsame[2C[1Bcode. The surface that matters is container-to-host, and th[63Gt's the s[73Gm[76Geither way. Warren reached the same plac[117G independently: [3m"isolation at the run granularity, not per-task or per-session."[23m[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mContext is pushed in, never pulled out.[43G[22mThis[48Gis[51Gthe[55Gpiece[61Gthat[66Gmakes[72Gleast[78Gprivilege[88Gactually[97Gwork.[103GHeart[109Gbuilds[116Gthe[120Gpacket[127Gand[131Gruns[136Gcapillaries'[149Gretrieval[159Gon[162Gthe[166Ghost,[172Gthen[177Gmounts[184Gthe[188Gresult[195Gread-only.[206GThe[210Gsubtask[218Greads[224Ga[226Gfile[231Gand[235Ghas[239Gno[242Gidea[247Ga[2C[1Bdatabase exists. Writes go out through the [47Gpool as[55Gappended NDJSON — the channe[84G already exists, it jus[109Gisn't load-bearing yet.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mThe sharpest hazard in your setup[37G[22mis[40G[38;2;177;185;249m/var/run/postgresql[39m.[61GPeer[66Gauth,[72Gempty[78Guser.[84GMount[90Git[93Gso[96Garteries[105Gworks[111Ginside[118Gthe[122Gcontainer[132Gand[136Gyou've[143Ghanded[150Gthe[154Gagent[160Gyour[165Gentire[172Gmemory[179Gstore.[186GThat[191Gmount[197Gis[200Gthe[204Gsingle[211Gmost[216Gtempting[225Gshortcut[234Gand[238Gthe[242Gone[246Gthat[2C[1Bvoids everything else.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOne real consequence for code we already changed.[53G[22m[38;2;177;185;249mlog_event[63G[39mfalls[69Gback[74Gto[77GJSONL[83Gand[87Gswallows[96Gthe[100Gfailure[108G—[110Ginside[117Ga[119Glocked-down[131Gcontainer[141Gthat[146Gwrites[153Ginto[158Ga[160Gfilesystem[171Gthat[176Gdies[181Gwith[186Git.[190GSilent[197Gtotal[203Gloss[208Gof[211Gevery[217Gsubtask's[227Gmemory.[235GThe[239Gspool[245Ghas[249Gto[2C[1Bbecome the primary write path for sandboxed runs before [38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[39m is worth having.[87GTh[90Gt's item 3 in th[108Gbu[111Gld order, and it's the one I'd start on.[K[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GCrunched for 3m 50s · 2 shells still running[1B[39m [3G                                            [215G[38;2;78;186;101m✔ Update installed · Restart to update[1B[38;2;8;145;178m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[48;2;8;145;178m[38;2;0;0;0m quality-assurance [49m[38;2;8;145;178m─[1B[39m❯ One episode can take longer so cap it at an hour instead, change workspace diffs to actual commits in heart. If there's a sandbox per episode, can permissions be changed for each spawned sandbox to apply least privilege access? What else needs to[K[1B  change in arteries to e[27Gsu[30Ge that sandboxes[47Gd[49Gn't conflict? Change spool to another[87Gname that's descriptive and[115Gintuitive[125Gfor its[133G