247Gsame[2C[1Bcode.[9GThe[13Gsurface[21Gthat[26Gmatters[34Gis[37Gcontainer-to-host,[56Gand[60Gthat's[67Gthe[71Gsame[76Geither[83Gway.[88GWarren[95Greached[103Gthe[107Gsame[112Gplace[118Gindependently:[133G[3m"isolation at the run granularity, not per-task or per-session."[2C[1B[23m[K[2C[1B[1mContext is pushed in, never pulled out.[22m This is the p[57Gece that makes lea[77G privilege ac[91Gually work.[103GHeart build[116Gthe packet and ru[134Gs[136Gc[138Gpillaries' retrieval[159Gon[162Gthe[166Ghost,[172Gthen[177Gmounts[184Gthe[188Gresult[195Gread-only.[206GThe[210Gsubtask[218Greads[224Ga[226Gfile[231Gand[235Ghas[239Gno[242Gidea[247Ga[2C[1Bdatabase[12Gexists.[20GWrites[27Ggo[30Gout[34Gthrough[42Gthe[46Gspool[52Gas[55Gappended[64GNDJSON[71G—[73Gthe[77Gchannel[85Galready[93Gexists,[101Git[104Gjust[109Gisn't[115Gload-bearing[128Gyet.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mThe sharpest hazard in your setup[37G[22mis [38;2;177;185;249m/var/run/postgresql[39m. Peer auth, e[74Gpty us[82G. Mount it so arteries works insid[118Gthe co[125Gtainer and you've handed the agent your entire memory store. That mount is[200Gthe[204Gsingle[211Gmost[216Gtempting[225Gshortcut[234Gand[238Gthe[242Gone[246Gthat[2C[1Bvoids[9Geverything[20Gelse.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOne real consequence for code we already changed.[22m [38;2;177;185;249mlog_event[39m falls back to[77GJSONL and sw[90Gllows the failure — i[112Gside [118G locked-down container[141Gthat[146Gwrites[153Ginto[158Ga[160Gfilesystem[171Gthat[176Gdies[181Gwith[186Git.[190GSilent[197Gtotal[203Gloss[208Gof[211Gevery[217Gsubtask's[227Gmemory.[235GThe[239Gspool[245Ghas[249Gto[2C[1Bbecome[10Gthe[14Gprimary[22Gwrite[28Gpath[33Gfor[37Gsandboxed[47Gruns[52Gbefore[59G[38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[70G[39mis[73Gworth[79Ghaving.[87GThat's[94Gitem[99G3[101Gin[104Gthe[108Gbuild[114Gorder,[121Gand[125Git's[130Gthe[134Gone[138GI'd[142Gstart[148Gon.[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GCrunched for 3m 50s · 2 shells still running[2B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mOne episode can take longer so cap it at an hour instead, change workspace diffs to actual commits in heart. If there's a sandbox per episode, can permissions be changed for each spawned sandbox to apply least privilege access? What else needs to [39m     [1B  [38;2;255;255;255mchange in across my stack to ensure that sandboxes don't conflict? Change spool to another name that's descriptive and intuitive for its function. Should worktrees be spawned throughout each episode/subtask since I'm trying to avoid being messy with [39m  [1B  [38;2;255;255;255mbranches while having enough isolation at the same time[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                     [1B[49m[K[1B[38;2;215;119;87m✽[3G[38;2;235;159;127mFi[38;2;215;119;87mddle-faddling… [215G[39m[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Tip: Did you know you can drag and drop image files into your terminal?[39m[K[1B     [7G       [15G   [19G    [24G      [31G  [34G   [38G  [41G  [44G  [47G    [52G        [61G      [68G         [78G     [84G  [87G      [94G       [102G  [105G      [112G  [115G       [123G [125G       [133G   [137G        [146G   [150G           [162G  [165G       [173G   [177G    [182G       [190G       [198G  [201G     [207G     [213G  [38;2;78;186;101m✔ Update installed · Restart to update[1B[38;2;8;145;178m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[48;2;8;145;178m[38;2;0;0;0m quality-assurance [49m[38;2;8;145;178m─[1