5G a run id[105Gper[109Gsubtask, [119Gocker-sbx contains th[141G episod[149G, arteries rememb[170Geach subtask separately.[195GTh[198G container[209Gis the only one of the four w[239Gth no identity[2C[1Bof its own — it's[21Ga runtime, not a scope. That's Mission[60GCon[64Grol's hard[75Gst-won lesson: th[93Gy[95Gmodel[103Gsandbox[111Gs as project scopes, and had to undo it.[K[2C[2B[1mThe container wraps the episode, not [41Ghe subtask.[22m Subtasks already [71Ghare a[78Gfilesyst[87Gm by design — the fix[109Gagent needs what the coder[136Gwrote. And pe[150G-subtask[159Gcon[163Gainer[169G buy no[177Gsecurity, beca[192Gse[195Gevery subtask has identic[221Gl perm[228Gssio[233Gs[235Gagai[240Gst the[247Gsame[2C[1Bcode. The surface that matters[34Gis contain[45Gr-t[49G-host, and that's the[71Gsame either way. W[90Grren reached the same place ind[122Gpendently:[133G[3m"isolation at the run granularity, not per-task or per-session."[2C[2B[23m[1mContext is pushed in, neve[31Gpulled out.[22m This is the piece[61Gthat[66Gmakes[72Gleast[78Gprivilege actually work. Heart bu[112Glds the pa[123Gke[126G a[129Gd ru[134Gs[136Gcapillaries' retrieval on the host,[172Gthen mounts the result read-only. The subtask reads a file and has no[242Gid[245Ga a[K[2C[1Bdatabase exists.[20GWrites[27Ggo[30Gout[34Gthrough[42Gthe[46Gspool[52Gas[55Gappended[64GNDJSON[71G—[73Gthe[77Gchannel[85Galready[93Gexists,[101Git[104Gjust[109Gisn't[115Gload-bearing[128Gyet.[2C[2B[1mTh[7Gsh[10Grpest hazard in your setup[22m is [38;2;177;185;249m/var/run/postgresql[39m. Peer auth, empty user. Mount it so[96Garteries works inside the container a[134Gd you've handed the agent[160Gyour en[168Gire memory [180Gtore.[186GThat mou[197Gis the single[211Gmost temp[221Ging [226Ghortcut and the [243Gne tha[250G[K[2C[1Bvoids everyth[17Gng else.[K[2B [3G[1mOne real consequence for code we already changed.[53G[22m[38;2;177;185;249mlog_event[63G[39mfalls[69Gback[74Gto[77GJSONL[83Gand[87Gswallows[96Gthe[100Gfailure[108G—[110Ginside[117Ga[119Glocked-down[131Gcontainer[141Gthat[146Gwrites[153Ginto[158Ga[160Gfilesystem[171Gthat[176Gdies[181Gwith[186Git.[190GSilent[197Gtotal[203Gloss[208Gof[211Gevery[217Gsubtask's[227Gmemory.[235GThe[239Gspool[245Ghas[249Gto[2C[1Bbecome[10Gthe[14Gprimary[22Gwrite[28Gpath[33Gfor[37Gsandboxed[47Gruns[52Gbefore[59G[38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[70G[39mis[73Gworth[79Ghaving.[87GThat's[94Gitem[99G3[101Gin[104Gthe[108Gbuild[114Gorder,[121Gand[125Git's[130Gthe[134Gone[138GI'd[142Gstart[148Gon.[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[39m [38;2;153;153;153mCrunched for 3m 50s · 2 shells still running[39m[K[1B[K[1B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mOne episode can take longer so cap it at an hour instead, change workspace diffs to actual commits in heart. If there's a sandbox per episode, can permissions be changed for each spawned sandbox to apply least privilege access? What else needs to [39m     [1B  [38;2;255;255;255mchange in across my stack to ensure that sandboxes don't conflict? Change spool to another name that's descriptive and intuitive for its function. Should worktrees be spawned throughout each episode/subtask since I'm trying to avoid being messy with [39m  [1B  [38;2;255;255;255mbranches while having enough isolation at the same time[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                     [2C[1B[49m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mSeveral[11Gthreads[19Ghere.[25GInvestigating[39Gthe[43Gtwo[47Gcode[52Gchanges[60Gfirst.[1B[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mRan [1m5[22m shell commands [2C[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mThree[9Gcode[14Gchanges.[23GStarting[32Gwith