-bearing ye[131G.[K[2B [3G[1mThe sharpest hazard in your setup[22m is [38;2;177;185;249m/var/run/postgresql[39m.[61GPeer[66Gauth,[72Gempty[78Guser.[84GMount[90Git[93Gso[96Garteries[105Gworks[111Ginside[118Gthe[122Gcontainer[132Gand[136Gyou've[143Ghanded[150Gthe[154Gagent[160Gyour[165Gentire[172Gmemory[179Gstore.[186GThat[191Gmount[197Gis[200Gthe[204Gsingle[211Gmost[216Gtempting[225Gshortcut[234Gand[238Gthe[242Gone[246Gthat[2C[1Bvoids[9Geverything[20Gelse.[1B[K[1B  [1mOne real consequence for code we already changed.[22m [38;2;177;185;249mlog_event[39m falls back to JSONL and swallows the failure — inside a locked-down container that writes into a filesystem that dies with it. Silent total loss of every subtask's memory. The spool has to[K[1B  become the primary write path for sandboxed runs before [38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[39m is worth having. That's item 3 in the build order, and it's the one I'd start on.[K[2B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GCrunched for 3m 50s · 2 shells still running[39m[K[2B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mOne episode can take longer so cap it at an hour instead, change workspace diffs to actual commits in heart. If there's a sandbox per episode, can permissions be changed for each spawned sandbox to apply least privilege access? What else needs to [39m     [1B  [38;2;255;255;255mchange in across my stack to ensure that sandboxes don't conflict? Change spool to another name that's descriptive and intuitive for its function. Should worktrees be spawned throughout each episode/subtask since I'm trying to avoid being messy with [39m  [1B  [38;2;255;255;255mbranches while having enough isolation at the same time[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                     [2B[49m[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mSeveral thre