48Git.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mThe container wraps the episode, not the subtask.[22m Subtasks [63Glready sh[73Gr[76Ga filesystem by design — the fix agent n[117Geds what the coder wrote. And per-subtask containers buy no security, because every[201Gsubtask[209Ghas[213Gidentical[223Gpermissions[235Gagainst[243Gthe[247Gsame[2C[1Bcode.[9GThe[13Gsurface[21Gthat[26Gmatters[34Gis[37Gcontainer-to-host,[56Gand[60Gthat's[67Gthe[71Gsame[76Geither[83Gway.[88GWarren[95Greached[103Gthe[107Gsame[112Gplace[118Gindependently:[133G[3m"isolation at the run granularity, not per-task or per-session."[2C[1B[23m[K[2C[1B[1mContext is pushed in, never pulled out.[22m Thi[47G is the[55Gpiece that makes least privi[84Gege actually work. Hear[109Gbuilds the packet and runs[136Gcapillaries'[149Gretrieval[159Gon[162Gthe[166Ghost,[172Gthen[177Gmounts[184Gthe[188Gresult[195Gread-only.[206GThe[210Gsubtask[218Greads[224Ga[226Gfile[231Gand[235Ghas[239Gno[242Gidea[247Ga[2C[1Bdatabase[12Gexists.[20GWrites[27Ggo[30Gout[34Gthrough[42Gthe[46Gspool[52Gas[55Gappended[64GNDJSON[71G—[73Gthe[77Gchannel[85Galready[93Gexists,[101Git[104Gjust[109Gisn't[115Gload-bearing[128Gyet.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mThe sharpest hazard in your setup[37G[22mis[40G[38;2;177;185;249m/var/run/postgresql[39m.[61GPeer[66Gauth,[72Gempty[78Guser.[84GMount[90Git[93Gso[96Garteries[105Gworks[111Ginside[118Gthe[122Gcontainer[132Gand[136Gyou've[143Ghanded[150Gthe[154Gagent[160Gyour[165Gentire[172Gmemory[179Gstore.[186GThat[191Gmount[197Gis[200Gthe[204Gsingle[211Gmost[216Gtempting[225Gshortcut[234Gand[238Gthe[242Gone[246Gthat[2C[1Bvoids[9Geverything[20Gelse.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOne real consequence for code we already changed.[22m [38;2;177;185;249mlog_event[39m falls back to JSONL and[87Gsw[90Gllows the failur[108G— [111Gnside a locked-down container that writes[153Ginto[158Ga[160Gfilesystem[171Gthat[176Gdies[181Gwith[186Git.[190GSilent[197Gtotal[203Gloss[208Gof[211Gevery[217Gsubtask's[227Gmemory.[235GThe[239Gspool[245Ghas[249Gto[2C[1Bbecome[10Gthe[14Gprimary[22Gwrite[28Gpath[33Gfor[37Gsandboxed[47Gruns[52Gbefore[59G[38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[70G[39mis[73Gworth[79Ghaving.[87GThat's[94Gitem[99G3[101Gin[104Gthe[108Gbuild[114Gorder,[121Gand[125Git's[130Gthe[134Gone[138GI'd[142Gstart[148Gon.[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GCrunched for 3m 50s · 2 shells still running[1B[39m[K[1B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mOne episode can take longer so cap i[40G [44Gan hour instead, change workspace diffs to ac[90Gual[94Gco[97Gmi[100Gs in heart. If there's a sandbox per episode, can[150Gpermissi[159Gns b[164G changed for each spawned sandbox to apply lea[211Gt privilege access? What[236Gelse ne[244Gd[246G to [39m   [2C[1B[38;2;255;255;255mch[7Gge in across my stack to[32Gensure that sandboxes[54Gdon't conflict? Change spool to another name that's descriptive and intuitive for its function. Should worktrees be spawned throughout each episode/subtask since I'm trying to avoid being messy with [1B[39m  [38;2;255;255;255mbranches while having enough isolation at the same time[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                     [1B[49m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mSeveral[11Gthreads[19Ghere.[25GInvestigating[39Gthe[43Gtwo[47Gcode[52Gchanges[60Gfirst.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mRan [1m5[22m shell commands [1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mThree[9Gcode[14Gchanges.[23GStarting[32Gwith[37Garteries:[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mRan [1m5[22m shell commands [1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mNow[7Gheart[13G—[15Gcommits[23Ginstead[31Gof[34Ga[36Gbare[41Gdi