[63G—[65Geach[70Gneeding[78Gits[82Gown[86Gbespoke[94Gworkaround[105G—[107Gthe[111Gboundary[120Gwould[126Gbe[129Gin[132Gthe[136Gwrong[142Gplace.[149GThey[154Garen't.[6C[2B[1msharpe[16Gway to see it[22m[K[2C[2B[1mThe gap list is a map of everywhere bwrap chose not to enforce a boundary.[78G[22m[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1Bbwrap[9Gbinds[15G[38;2;177;185;249m~/.claude[39m,[26G[38;2;177;185;249m~/.codex[39m,[36G[38;2;177;185;249m~/.config[46G[39mwritable[55Gand[59Gleaves[66Gthe[70Gnetwork[78Gshared[85G—[87Gits[91Gown[95Gdocstring[105Gsays[110Gso:[114G[3m"Network stays shared (agents call APIs)"[156G[23mand[160G[3m"containment for accidents and reward hacking, not a security boundary against a hostile [2C[1Bmodel."[23m[K[2C[2BEvery hard[14Ggap is exactly[29Gone of thos[42Gconc[47Gss[50Go[52Gs.[55Gbwrap[61Gkept the functi[77Gnality by ke[90Gping[95Gthe hol[103G.[105G[38;2;177;185;249mdocker-sbx[116G[39mcl[119Gses[124Ghe h[129Gle, so[136Gthe functionality[154Ghas to b[164Grebuilt [173Gs [176Gomething[185Gthat[190Gcrosses[198Ga[200Gboundary[209Gdeliberately.[2C[2BThat's the real work, and[29Git's[34Gwhy[38Gthe[42Ganswer[49Gisn't[55G"make[61Gthe[65Gcontainer[75Gmore[80Gpermissive."[93GA[95Gcontainer[105Gpermissive[116Genough[123Gto[126Gavoid[132Gall[136Gof[139Gthis[144G[3mis[147G[23mbwrap,[154Gwith[159Gmore[164Gmoving[171Gparts.[2C[2B[1mThe gaps that aren't this[22m[K[2C[2BThree are just missing infrastruc[37Gu[40G,[46Gwould[52Gapply to any[65Gcontainer: the image [87Goesn't exist, the daemo[111G isn't running, and Docker[138GDesktop's VM bin[155G-mount[162Gbehaviour[172Gis[175Guntested.[185GThose[191Gare[195Gsetup,[202Gnot[206Gdesign.[2C[2BOne was my bug: the timeout was stored[42Gand[46Gnever[52Genforced,[62Gso[65Ga[67Ghung[72Gcontainer[82Gwould[88Ghave[93Goutlived[102Gthe[106Gclient[113Gh[144Gslot.[150GFixed.[